# ============================================================================
# GLOWanalyses root .gitignore (standalone workflow-template repository)
#
# GLOWanalyses ships as a standalone repo (the release tree carries this file).
# In the GLOWpipeline monorepo these patterns are provided by the monorepo-root
# .gitignore; the standalone repo needs its own copy so a fresh clone that RUNS
# the bundled example does not show regenerated outputs as untracked. The nested
# data-example/.gitignore handles the synthetic cohort's tracked-vs-generated
# split (and its `!` re-includes assume the global *.rds / *.csv ignore below).
#
# File Log (reverse chronological order):
# - 2026-06-14: Created by Claude Code (Opus 4.8 / 1M ctx, r-developer agent),
#   prompted by ZWu (release cleanup). Adds the standalone-repo ignores that the
#   monorepo-root .gitignore used to provide: per-run outputs/, the data-example
#   generated lineage dirs, and the global *.rds / *.csv ignore that the nested
#   data-example/.gitignore's force-tracks depend on.
# ============================================================================

# ---- R / editor cruft ------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.DS_Store
Rplots.pdf

# ---- Large data files (the data-example tracked .rds/.csv assets are force-
#      tracked back in via data-example/.gitignore's `!` re-includes) ---------
*.rds
*.csv

# ---- Per-run generated outputs (regenerated by the stages / run-example.sh).
#      A run lives at runs/<run>/<stage>/, so its outputs/ is one or two levels
#      deep; cover both. ------------------------------------------------------
runs/*/outputs/
runs/*/*/outputs/

# ---- data-example generated lineage dirs (also covered by the nested
#      data-example/.gitignore; listed here so the root is self-contained). The
#      pre-built aGDS under example_gds_favor/flexible/gds/ is TRACKED and is NOT
#      a lineage dir, so it is unaffected. -----------------------------------
data-example/cohort/example_gds/
data-example/cohort/example_pcs/
data-example/cohort/example_pheno/
data-example/cohort/example_ld/
